{"availability":"available","full":"thevpc/nuts","name":"nuts","description":"Nuts Java Package Manager","category":"Developer tools","language":"Java","stars":160,"forks":6,"created":"2017-07-24T08:51:47Z","updated":"2026-10-11T09:50:23Z","license":null,"branch":"master","homepage":"https://thevpc.github.io/nuts/","topics":["devops","java","maven","package-manager"],"demo":"https://thevpc.github.io/nuts/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T06:27:27.055Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T06:27:27.055Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T06:27:27.055Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:53:23.367Z","stars":160,"forks":6},{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:26.813Z","stars":160,"forks":6},{"at":"2026-10-12T06:27:27.055Z","stars":160,"forks":6}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Nuts is a package manager for Java applications that focuses on the application lifecycle and isolated deployments.","Nuts manages dependencies at runtime, not at build time, by reusing Maven descriptors directly and solving the long-standing fat-jars problem efficiently:","Nuts does not require any custom descriptors or build tools, does not change classloading behavior, it just solves dependency tree, builds the classpath and runs the application."],"features":["It downloads only the JARs and dependencies that are actually needed on the target machine","Similarly, for native binaries, it retains only assets relevant for the target platform.","Works with existing Maven JARs — zero repackaging","Supports multiple repositories simultaneously, including Maven-central and Maven-compatible repositories","Full application lifecycle — Install, run, update, and uninstall applications — with multiple versions coexisting in the same workspace"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/thevpc/nuts/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"5d910aa4131dc635443d7589c7cc2e06c8a2066e4084408ce83b5ffe4b52bbfd","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:23.722Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T